{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>were broken up, all the fountains of the great deep.</b> \"Fountains\" is in construct, as in \"when there were no fountains\" (Proverbs 8:24) — it is well-known." "<b>The deep.</b> Masculine and feminine, likewise \"the deep made it grow tall\" (Ezekiel 31:4). And He did not mention the rivers, for they issued from the fountains. And when they were broken open, the waters rose, and the windows of the storehouses in the heaven were opened, and the waters came down and the earth was inundated, and there was no distinction between day and night — the proof is that it says, \"day and night they shall not cease\" (Genesis 8:22). And when the waters of the heaven were cut off, then Noah knew that forty days and forty nights had passed, for HaShem had revealed this secret to him." "<b>And the windows.</b> Like \"Behold, YHWH makes windows\" (II Kings 7:2). And \"storehouse\" and \"window\" are according to the language of people and their usage. Some say the alef is a root letter, like כבודות. Others say the alef is added, like the alef of אגורת (I Samuel 2:36), and they are from doubled-root formations. And on the seventeenth day, when the flood began, Noah and his household entered the ark and brought into it the beasts and the cattle and the creeping things and the birds. And the word <b>bird</b> is a general term for whatever has a wing. And the wonder is that all of them came of themselves, two by two."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra leaves his grammatical dispute about ארבות (windows) incomplete: he notes the alef may be a root letter (comparing כבודות, taking ארבות as a plural like it) or added (comparing אגורת, where alef is prosthetic), but does not resolve which. 'Doubled-root formations' (מפעלי הכפל) renders his classification of forms built on a doubled stem."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:44.031451604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}